   "stem": {
      "text": "Consider the curve y^3 - 3y = x^2 - 4x, for which dy/dx = (2x - 4)/(3y^2 - 3). How many points on the curve have a vertical tangent line?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 4
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "A vertical tangent needs the denominator to be zero with the numerator nonzero: 3y^2 - 3 = 0 gives y = 1 or y = -1.",
         "mathjson": 1
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Substitute y = 1 into the curve: -2 = x^2 - 4x, so x^2 - 4x + 2 = 0 and x = 2 + sqrt(2) or x = 2 - sqrt(2).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            2,
            [
               "Sqrt",
               2
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Substitute y = -1: 2 = x^2 - 4x, so x^2 - 4x - 2 = 0 and x = 2 + sqrt(6) or x = 2 - sqrt(6).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            2,
            [
               "Sqrt",
               6
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "None of the four x-values equals 2, so the numerator 2x - 4 is nonzero at every one of them. The curve has 4 points with a vertical tangent.",
         "mathjson": 4
      }
   ],
